 " is a fibered graph: a total graph with a projection defined on all its \
vertices.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"2f3da8b5-f9fd-4989-952f-159500cad192"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A fibered graph is a graph ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 " with a map ",
 StyleBox["\[Pi]", "TI"],
 " on its vertices. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraFiberedGraphQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFiberedGraphQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "75eb0adb-dede-4ad9-8691-bc48175b5212"],
 " tests only that ",
 StyleBox["\[Pi]", "TI"],
 " is defined on every vertex of ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4f7e0a33-c7b9-45aa-9ee4-503bc62802d1"],

Cell["\<\
The total graph must be finite, simple, undirected, unweighted and without \
edge tags. The projection is an association with one key for each vertex, or \
a function.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2d0799f2-46ea-4312-aeb5-d949d2b5dc7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "No further condition is tested. Fibers of different sizes, vertical edges \
and vertices without lifts are allowed; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraFibrationQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFibrationQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ac33bd95-a020-4c3e-8d97-560bb07b2968"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraFiberBundleQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFiberBundleQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "93b2302b-db88-4f7f-ba02-b5ba6b8bd808"],
 " test those."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4c13f208-ad42-4ba7-8e77-0c1fbc635137"],

